# {{PROJECT_NAME}}: rules for agents

Unreal Engine project, engine association `{{ENGINE_ASSOCIATION}}`. These rules apply to every agent
and every person working in this repository. Machine-specific notes (engine path, personal
permissions) go in a gitignored local file, never here.

## Layout

| Path | What |
|---|---|
| `Source/{{PROJECT_NAME}}/` | All gameplay code (C++). Plain-C++ rules under `Rules/`, tests under `Tests/` |
| `Content/{{PROJECT_NAME}}/` | Everything the game ships. Nothing shipped lives outside it |
| `Config/` | Engine, game and input settings |
| `scripts/editor/` | Editor Python scripts: re-runnable, absolute paths resolved at run time |
| `docs/` | Design, roadmap, devlog, `MCP_TOOLS.md` |
| `SourceArt/` | Source images, audio, meshes and their generator scripts |

## Working rules

1. Start with `git pull --rebase` and `git status`. Commit small, with explicit paths. Never force-push.
2. Gameplay logic is C++. Blueprint and widget assets are thin subclasses holding asset references
   and tuning. Data lives in CSV or JSON under version control.
3. Never edit `.uasset` or `.umap` files outside the editor. One person or agent edits a given level
   at a time.
4. Reflection changes (new or changed `UCLASS`, `USTRUCT`, `UPROPERTY`, `UFUNCTION`, new files,
   `Build.cs`) need a closed editor and a full build. Live Coding is for function bodies only.
5. After any scripted or MCP edit: save, check nothing is left unsaved, and confirm the change in
   `git status`. Graph tools compile Blueprints but do not save them.
6. Build and package only when asked. Never build while an editor or game of this project runs.
7. Everything shipped stays inside `/Game/{{PROJECT_NAME}}/`. Check the dependency closure of each
   shipping map before calling content done.
8. Every third-party asset and AI tool goes in the credits file with its licence. Assets whose
   licence forbids AI use are placed by code only; agents do not open, edit or copy them.
9. Read the clock before writing a time. Do not estimate it.

## Definition of done

1. Compiles with no new warnings from this project's modules.
2. Logic: `{{PROJECT_NAME}}.*` automation tests pass.
3. Visual: a screenshot read at full size, with a one-line verdict.
4. Gameplay: the changed step ran in PIE or self-play through the real input path.
5. Saved and visible in `git status`; committed; one line in `docs/DEVLOG.md`.
6. The report says what was not verified.

## Testing

- Self-play: `{{PROJECT_NAME}}.exe -AutoPlay -Seed=1` plays, logs `AUTOPLAY PASS|FAIL <name>` lines,
  saves screenshots and quits. Automated runs start from default settings and save none.
- A build reaches a human only after its tests pass on the packaged build.
- A human finding that no test caught becomes a new test.
